window.CET6_DATA("data/articles/day-005.json",{"day":5,"title":"Who Gets to Tell a Town’s Story?","targetWords":[{"word":"partner","gloss":"伙伴","context":"We paired each volunteer with a partner and invited residents to lend photographs.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"native","gloss":"本地人","context":"As a native of the town, I had assumed that its museum represented everybody.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"gender","gloss":"社会性别","context":"Our new account separated biological sex from the assumptions attached to gender.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"citizen","gloss":"公民","context":"A guest might enjoy the display of a king or a military hero, yet an ordinary citizen could fail to recognize her own identity in it.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"son","gloss":"儿子","context":"A son brought an image of his mother holding an infant shortly after birth.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"whom","gloss":"谁","context":"Our history committee began to ask whom the collection included, and whom it silently left outside.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"being","gloss":"人","context":"An adolescent spoke about being the victim of public ridicule, and another resident paused to catch her breath before describing a violent childhood.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"identity","gloss":"身份","context":"A guest might enjoy the display of a king or a military hero, yet an ordinary citizen could fail to recognize her own identity in it.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"ourselves","gloss":"我们自己","context":"Instead, we had allowed ourselves to see the town as a place built by many hands.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"guest","gloss":"客人","context":"A guest might enjoy the display of a king or a military hero, yet an ordinary citizen could fail to recognize her own identity in it.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"blood","gloss":"血","context":"Stories of youth stood beside accounts of old age, and a blood relationship was no longer the only source of belonging.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"herself","gloss":"她自己","context":"The teenager looked for a photograph of someone like herself and found none.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"household","gloss":"家庭","context":"Then my younger brother brought a classmate whose household had recently arrived from abroad.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"brother","gloss":"兄弟","context":"Then my younger brother brought a classmate whose household had recently arrived from abroad.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"teenager","gloss":"青少年","context":"The teenager looked for a photograph of someone like herself and found none.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"crowd","gloss":"人群","context":"One photograph showed a giant crowd beside a factory.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"relative","gloss":"亲戚","context":"A daughter described a neighbor who helped with childcare, while a sister recalled a relative who had been forced to work as a slave.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"sex","gloss":"生理性别","context":"Our new account separated biological sex from the assumptions attached to gender.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"birth","gloss":"出生","context":"A son brought an image of his mother holding an infant shortly after birth.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"king","gloss":"君主","context":"A guest might enjoy the display of a king or a military hero, yet an ordinary citizen could fail to recognize her own identity in it.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"giant","gloss":"巨大的","context":"One photograph showed a giant crowd beside a factory.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"youth","gloss":"青春","context":"Stories of youth stood beside accounts of old age, and a blood relationship was no longer the only source of belonging.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"daughter","gloss":"女儿","context":"A daughter described a neighbor who helped with childcare, while a sister recalled a relative who had been forced to work as a slave.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"volunteer","gloss":"志愿者","context":"We paired each volunteer with a partner and invited residents to lend photographs.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"affair","gloss":"事务","context":"The archive had treated each account as a private affair.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"victim","gloss":"受害者","context":"An adolescent spoke about being the victim of public ridicule, and another resident paused to catch her breath before describing a violent childhood.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"nobody","gloss":"谁也不","context":"Nobody could understand its past by studying famous names alone.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"sister","gloss":"姐妹","context":"A daughter described a neighbor who helped with childcare, while a sister recalled a relative who had been forced to work as a slave.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"skin","gloss":"皮肤","context":"Hair, skin, and clothing were visible, but courage and skill could not be inferred from them.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"everybody","gloss":"每人","context":"As a native of the town, I had assumed that its museum represented everybody.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"hair","gloss":"头发","context":"Hair, skin, and clothing were visible, but courage and skill could not be inferred from them.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"arm","gloss":"手臂","context":"At its core stood a young worker with a strong arm and a torn sleeve; a fellow employee rested a hand on his shoulder.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"hero","gloss":"英雄","context":"A guest might enjoy the display of a king or a military hero, yet an ordinary citizen could fail to recognize her own identity in it.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"muscle","gloss":"肌肉","context":"An old caption praised masculine muscle, but ignored the female workers at the edge of the frame.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"adolescent","gloss":"青少年","context":"An adolescent spoke about being the victim of public ridicule, and another resident paused to catch her breath before describing a violent childhood.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"infant","gloss":"婴幼儿","context":"A son brought an image of his mother holding an infant shortly after birth.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"host","gloss":"主持人","context":"As host of one session, I reminded myself that a human being was offering trust, not raw material for an exhibition.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"elite","gloss":"精英","context":"Even the supposed elite had depended on people absent from official portraits.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"myself","gloss":"我自己","context":"As host of one session, I reminded myself that a human being was offering trust, not raw material for an exhibition.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"breath","gloss":"呼吸","context":"An adolescent spoke about being the victim of public ridicule, and another resident paused to catch her breath before describing a violent childhood.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"counterpart","gloss":"同行","context":"My counterpart at a neighboring museum, a collaborator rather than a rival, advised us to return control to the speakers: each could remove a sentence, correct an error, or withdraw an image.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"pair","gloss":"一对","context":"When the exhibition reopened, a pair of schoolchildren traced a family route on a map with one finger.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"slave","gloss":"奴隶","context":"A daughter described a neighbor who helped with childcare, while a sister recalled a relative who had been forced to work as a slave.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"finger","gloss":"手指","context":"When the exhibition reopened, a pair of schoolchildren traced a family route on a map with one finger.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"neighbor","gloss":"邻居","context":"A daughter described a neighbor who helped with childcare, while a sister recalled a relative who had been forced to work as a slave.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"rival","gloss":"竞争对手","context":"My counterpart at a neighboring museum, a collaborator rather than a rival, advised us to return control to the speakers: each could remove a sentence, correct an error, or withdraw an image.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"core","gloss":"中心","context":"At its core stood a young worker with a strong arm and a torn sleeve; a fellow employee rested a hand on his shoulder.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"fellow","gloss":"同事的","context":"At its core stood a young worker with a strong arm and a torn sleeve; a fellow employee rested a hand on his shoulder.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"shoulder","gloss":"肩膀","context":"At its core stood a young worker with a strong arm and a torn sleeve; a fellow employee rested a hand on his shoulder.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"classmate","gloss":"同学","context":"Then my younger brother brought a classmate whose household had recently arrived from abroad.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null}],"paragraphs":[{"en":"As a native of the town, I had assumed that its museum represented everybody. Then my younger brother brought a classmate whose household had recently arrived from abroad. The teenager looked for a photograph of someone like herself and found none. A guest might enjoy the display of a king or a military hero, yet an ordinary citizen could fail to recognize her own identity in it. Our history committee began to ask whom the collection included, and whom it silently left outside.","zh":"作为本地人，我曾以为镇上的博物馆代表了所有人。后来，弟弟带来一位同学，她一家刚从国外搬来。这位少女想找到与自己相似的人物照片，却一张也没找到。游客可能喜欢有关国王或军事英雄的展览，但普通居民也可能在其中看不到自己的身份。于是，历史委员会开始追问：藏品包括了谁，又默默地把谁排除在外？"},{"en":"We paired each volunteer with a partner and invited residents to lend photographs. A son brought an image of his mother holding an infant shortly after birth. A daughter described a neighbor who helped with childcare, while a sister recalled a relative who had been forced to work as a slave. The archive had treated each account as a private affair. In reality, these memories revealed how power, labor, and care shaped the town. Nobody could understand its past by studying famous names alone.","zh":"我们让志愿者结成搭档，并邀请居民借出照片。一位儿子带来母亲产后不久抱着婴儿的照片。一位女儿讲述邻居帮忙照顾孩子的往事，一位姐姐回忆曾被迫充当奴隶的亲人。档案馆过去把这些故事视为私人事务。事实上，这些记忆揭示了权力、劳动与照护如何塑造城镇。仅研究名人的名字，没人能真正理解这里的过去。"},{"en":"One photograph showed a giant crowd beside a factory. At its core stood a young worker with a strong arm and a torn sleeve; a fellow employee rested a hand on his shoulder. An old caption praised masculine muscle, but ignored the female workers at the edge of the frame. Our new account separated biological sex from the assumptions attached to gender. Hair, skin, and clothing were visible, but courage and skill could not be inferred from them. Even the supposed elite had depended on people absent from official portraits.","zh":"一张照片呈现了工厂旁的大群人。人群中央是个胳膊结实、袖子破了的年轻工人，工友把手搭在他肩上。旧说明文字赞扬了男性的力量，却忽略了画面边缘的女工。新的叙述区分生理性别与附加在性别上的社会假设。头发、肤色与衣着可以看见，勇气和技能却无法从中推断。即便所谓精英，也依赖那些缺席于正式肖像的人。"},{"en":"The interviews sometimes required restraint. An adolescent spoke about being the victim of public ridicule, and another resident paused to catch her breath before describing a violent childhood. We did not press for dramatic details. As host of one session, I reminded myself that a human being was offering trust, not raw material for an exhibition. My counterpart at a neighboring museum, a collaborator rather than a rival, advised us to return control to the speakers: each could remove a sentence, correct an error, or withdraw an image.","zh":"访谈有时需要克制。一位少年讲到自己曾遭受公开嘲笑，另一位居民在叙述充满暴力的童年之前，停下来平复呼吸。我们没有追问戏剧性的细节。作为一场访谈的主持人，我提醒自己：一个活生生的人是在交付信任，而不是提供展览素材。邻近博物馆的同行是合作者而非竞争对手，他建议把控制权还给讲述者：他们可以删掉一句话、纠正错误，或收回照片。"},{"en":"When the exhibition reopened, a pair of schoolchildren traced a family route on a map with one finger. Stories of youth stood beside accounts of old age, and a blood relationship was no longer the only source of belonging. We had not made every account agree. Instead, we had allowed ourselves to see the town as a place built by many hands. The greatest change was that visitors began asking not which single person represented the community, but how its different lives connected. The committee kept a record of unresolved questions so that future volunteers could challenge its choices, ensuring that a more inclusive exhibition would remain open to correction rather than become another final authority.","zh":"展览重新开放时，两个孩子用手指在地图上追踪一家人的迁居路线。青春的故事与晚年的叙述并列，血缘也不再是归属的唯一来源。我们并没有让所有叙述彼此一致，而是让自己看到，这座城镇由许多人的双手共同建成。最大的变化在于，游客开始追问：不是哪一个人代表社区，而是不同人生怎样相互联系。委员会保留尚未解决的问题，让未来的志愿者可以质疑其选择，确保更包容的展览仍接受修正，而不成为另一种终局权威。"}],"previous":4,"next":6});
